§§ `1.15 — the time in use of the vehicle`

-- Counted in whole months, from the month of first registration in Vietnam (or, for a
-- vehicle imported after use abroad, from January of its year of manufacture) to the month
-- the contract was concluded. Fork F9: "from month A to month B" is B minus A, not B minus A
-- plus one. The defined term is not used again in the rules:
-- 13.2 says "Thời gian đã sử dụng" and 14.1.2(b) says "Xe sử dụng";
-- both are read as this term (fork F10, finding X11).
-- src:126 | 1.15. “Thời Gian Sử Dụng Xe Ô Tô” là khoảng thời gian tính từ tháng đăng ký lần
-- src:127 | đầu tại Việt Nam đến tháng giao kết Hợp Đồng Bảo Hiểm. Đối với Xe Ô Tô nhập
-- src:128 | khẩu đã qua sử dụng ở nước ngoài, thời gian sử dụng tính từ tháng một của
-- src:129 | năm sản xuất đến tháng giao kết Hợp Đồng Bảo Hiểm.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the month number of` d MEANS (DATE_YEAR d TIMES 12) PLUS DATE_MONTH d

@ref O-Car rules, Article 1.15 (src:126-129)
GIVEN p IS A `The policy`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`1.15 — the month the time in use is counted from` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p's `vehicle`'s `origin`
    WHEN `imported after use abroad` THEN (p's `vehicle`'s `year of manufacture` TIMES 12) PLUS 1
    OTHERWISE `the month number of` (p's `vehicle`'s `date of first registration in Vietnam`)

@ref O-Car rules, Article 1.15 (src:126-129)
GIVEN p IS A `The policy`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`1.15 — the time in use of the vehicle, in months` p MEANS
    `the month number of` (p's `date the contract was concluded`)
    MINUS `1.15 — the month the time in use is counted from` p

§ `Counting days`

-- The rules count periods in "ngày làm việc" (working days: 3.1.3, 3.2.1, 4.2, 5.2, 6),
-- in "ngày" (days: 3.2.2, 3.2.3, 6, 10, 16.1.1), in "giờ" (hours: 5.2) and in "năm" (years:
-- 10). They define none of these. Which days are not working days is a calendar the caller
-- supplies, weekends and public holidays alike (fork F8); a period "kể từ ngày X" does not
-- count day X itself (fork F7).

-- The serial number of a day, so that two dates can be subtracted.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the day number of` d MEANS Day d

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `days after` d MEANS Date (Day d PLUS n)

-- The date on which a period of n working days, counted from day d, ends.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
      `the non-working days` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the end of` n `working days counted from` d `skipping` `the non-working days` MEANS
    IF   n AT MOST 0
    THEN d
    ELSE IF   elem `the next day` `the non-working days`
         THEN `the end of` n           `working days counted from` `the next day` `skipping` `the non-working days`
         ELSE `the end of` (n MINUS 1) `working days counted from` `the next day` `skipping` `the non-working days`
    WHERE
        `the next day` MEANS Date (Day d PLUS 1)

-- The same period as a number of calendar days after day d, for a WITHIN clause.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
      `the non-working days` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the calendar days in` n `working days counted from` d `skipping` `the non-working days` MEANS
    Day (`the end of` n `working days counted from` d `skipping` `the non-working days`) MINUS Day d

§ `The two versions of the rules`

-- The heading: rules issued by Decision 124/2019 of 31/12/2019, amended by the supplementary
-- clauses issued by Decision 17/2022 of 28/03/2022.
-- src:5 | (Quy tắc điều khoản sản phẩm được ban hành theo Quyết định số 124/2019/QĐ-TGĐ ngày
-- src:6 | 31/12/2019 và được sửa đổi theo Điều khoản bảo hiểm bổ sung được ban hành theo Quyết định
-- src:7 | số 17/2022/QĐ-TGĐ ngày 28/03/2022 của Tổng Giám đốc Công ty Cổ phần Bảo hiểm OPES)
--
-- WHAT THE FILE CONTAINS. Articles 1-17 (src:55-986), then the supplementary clauses
-- BS01-BS07 under their own heading (src:998-1129), then an undated clause on personal data
-- (src:1141-1249). The 2022 amendment is the supplementary clauses: they sit apart from
-- Articles 1-17 and say themselves which base provisions they cancel (BS03 cancels 12.12,
-- BS04 cancels 14.1.2(a), BS05 cancels 12.15). Whether Decision 17/2022 also edited the text
-- of Articles 1-17 the file does not show, and no 2019 text is in the sources: this encoding
-- takes Articles 1-17 as printed to be the 2019 text (fork F2).
--
-- WHICH VERSION GOVERNS A POLICY: the one in force when the contract was concluded (fork
-- F1), taking each Decision to be in force from its own date, which is the only date the
-- file gives (fork F2). Before 31/12/2019 the file says nothing, and that is declined.

`the date of Decision 124/2019` MEANS YMD 2019 12 31
`the date of Decision 17/2022`  MEANS YMD 2022 3 28

@ref O-Car rules, heading (src:5-7) — no version of the rules before Decision 124/2019 is in the document
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`no version of the rules before Decision 124/2019 of 31/12/2019 is in the document` MEANS
    REFUSE "no version of the rules before Decision 124/2019 of 31/12/2019 is in the document"

@ref O-Car rules, heading (src:5-7); NOTES.md forks F1, F2
GIVEN p IS A `The policy`
GIVETH A `The version of the rules`
`the version of the rules governing` p MEANS
    BRANCH IF p's `date the contract was concluded` AT LEAST `the date of Decision 17/2022`  THEN `the rules as amended by the supplementary clauses of Decision 17/2022`
           IF p's `date the contract was concluded` AT LEAST `the date of Decision 124/2019` THEN `the rules as made by Decision 124/2019`
           OTHERWISE `no version of the rules before Decision 124/2019 of 31/12/2019 is in the document`

@ref O-Car rules, heading (src:5-7)
GIVEN p IS A `The policy`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the supplementary clauses of Decision 17/2022 govern` p MEANS
    CONSIDER `the version of the rules governing` p
    WHEN `the rules as amended by the supplementary clauses of Decision 17/2022` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the rules as made by Decision 124/2019` THEN FALSE
